---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<SiteLayout title="FAQ — Altara" description="Answers to the questions we hear most about planning, visas, health and travel to Bhutan with Altara.">
<!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
  <section class="hero hero--page hero--center"
    style="background-image:url('/assets/images/image/Wangdue2.webp');background-position:center 45%;">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1>FAQ</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-mist" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="hero-mist-layer hero-mist-layer--1" style="background-image:url('/assets/images/cloud.webp');"></div>
      <div class="hero-mist-layer hero-mist-layer--2" style="background-image:url('/assets/images/cloud.webp');"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= INTRO ================= -->
  <section class="info-lead reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Still Deciding</span>
      <h2>Everything We Get<br>Asked Most</h2>
      <p>From what a trip actually costs to what to pack for a mountain pass, here's what past travelers have
        wanted to know before booking with us. Can't find your question? <a href="#enquire"
          class="faq-contact-link">Contact us</a> directly and we'll answer it personally.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
  <section class="faq reveal">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="faq-category">
        <div class="faq-category-head">
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Planning Your Trip</span>
          <h2>Planning &amp; Booking</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-columns">
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What's the difference between booking directly through Altara and going through a travel
                  agent abroad?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Booking directly means your itinerary is designed by the people who actually run it on the
                  ground in Bhutan — no markup, no middleman, and a planner who knows every guide and route
                  personally.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What does it cost to visit Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Every journey is quoted individually based on season, pace, and accommodation, since Bhutan has
                  no fixed daily package rate — on top of that, every visitor pays the government's Sustainable
                  Development Fee directly. See our <a href="/tariff" class="faq-contact-link">Tariff page</a>
                  for the current figures.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>How is Altara different from other Bhutan operators?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>We only work in Bhutan, only plan private departures, and build every trip around how you want
                  to feel — not a fixed template of sights to check off.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>When is the best time to travel in Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Spring (March–May) and autumn (September–November) bring the clearest skies and the major
                  tshechu festivals, though winter offers rare stillness and near-empty monasteries for those who
                  prefer quiet. More detail on our <a href="/about-bhutan" class="faq-contact-link">About
                    Bhutan page</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-category">
        <div class="faq-category-head">
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Getting In</span>
          <h2>Visa &amp; Entry</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-columns">
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Do I need a visa to visit Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Most nationalities do, and it's arranged for you through Altara once your trip is confirmed —
                  there's no need to deal with an embassy yourself. Travelers from India, Bangladesh and the
                  Maldives don't need a visa, only a permit.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What is the Sustainable Development Fee?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>A per-night fee paid directly to the Bhutanese government, funding free healthcare, education
                  and conservation for its citizens. Full current rates are on our <a href="/tariff"
                    class="faq-contact-link">Tariff page</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>How do I actually fly into Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Only two airlines land in Bhutan, both into Paro — one of the most technically demanding
                  approaches in the world, flown only in daylight, good weather. We handle your flight
                  arrangements as part of planning your itinerary.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Is Bhutan safe to visit?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Bhutan is consistently ranked among the safest countries in Asia for travelers, with very low
                  crime rates. The main things to plan around are altitude and mountain roads, not personal safety.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-category">
        <div class="faq-category-head">
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">Before You Pack</span>
          <h2>Health &amp; Practical</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-columns">
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Would we need travel insurance?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes — comprehensive travel insurance covering medical evacuation is required for entry into
                  Bhutan, and we can recommend providers suited to the altitudes and regions on your route.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>Is altitude sickness a concern?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Most of Bhutan's towns sit between 1,200m and 2,700m, which is comfortable for almost everyone.
                  It only becomes a real consideration on higher treks like the Snowman or Jomolhari, and we pace
                  those itineraries with acclimatization in mind.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-column">
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What's the cancellation policy for travel to Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Terms scale with how close to departure you cancel and are confirmed in writing before booking,
                  so there are never surprises — ask your planner for the specifics of your itinerary.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                <span>What should I pack for Bhutan?</span>
                <span class="faq-icon"></span>
              </button>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Layers, whatever the season — mornings and evenings are cool even in summer. Modest dress is
                  expected at dzongs and monasteries (covered shoulders and knees), and comfortable, broken-in
                  walking shoes matter more than anything technical unless you're trekking.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= DARK CTA ================= -->
  <section class="dark-cta dark-cta--photo reveal" id="enquire"
    style="background-image:url('/assets/images/image/prayer flag.webp');">
    <div class="dark-cta-inner">
      <h2>Begin Your Journey</h2>
      <p>Still have a question of your own? Share a little about how you'd like to feel, and our team will shape a
        private Bhutan journey around it — no templates, no packages.</p>
      <div class="dark-cta-ctas">
        <a href="https://wa.me/9752333456" class="contact-pill" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path
              d="M21 11.5a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9 3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1-7.6 4.7 8.38 8.38 0 0 1-3.8-.9L3 20l1.9-5.7a8.38 8.38 0 0 1-.9-3.8 8.5 8.5 0 0 1 4.7-7.6 8.38 8.38 0 0 1 3.8-.9h.5a8.48 8.48 0 0 1 8 8v.5z" />
          </svg>
          <span>WhatsApp Us</span>
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:hello@altara.travel" class="contact-pill">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" />
            <path d="M3 7l9 6 9-6" />
          </svg>
          <span>Mail Us</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
